    "content": "Product Version: 2.0.0 Document Classification: Enterprise Software Documentation Documentation Status: Official Release Last Updated: November 2026 Welcome to the official documentation portal for PortProbe , the enterprise-grade asynchronous TCP connectivity verification daemon and client probe written in Rust. --- Navigation Directory The PortProbe documentation package is organized into dedicated topic sections: --- Documentation Conventions Throughout this documentation, the following formatting conventions are used: !NOTE Highlights background context, operational recommendations, or important behavioral characteristics. !TIP Suggests performance optimizations, security hardening best practices, or command-line shortcuts. !IMPORTANT Emphasizes critical operational steps, mandatory configuration parameters, or security invariants. !WARNING Identifies dangerous configurations, potential operational pitfalls, or security risks. !CAUTION Alerts to high-risk actions that could result in service disruption, denial of service, or security exposure. --- Verifiability and Source Code Fidelity Every command, configuration key, flag, and code snippet in this documentation has been verified against the PortProbe version 2.0.0 codebase src/main.rs , src/cli.rs , src/server.rs , src/logger.rs . Features marked as Implemented reflect fully functional code supported by automated test suites. Features marked as Operational Workaround or Planned Roadmap represent known implementation boundaries such as Windows Service integration or UDP prober support and are explicitly identified to maintain strict engineering integrity."
