    "content": "Document Reference: PORTPROBE-DOC-GS-01 Document Version: 2.0.0 Classification: Getting Started Guide Status: Official Release Last Updated: November 2026 --- 1. Supported Operating Systems PortProbe is engineered for cross-platform enterprise infrastructure. Supported platforms include: | Operating System | Architecture | Support Tier | Deployment Method | Notes | | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Linux RHEL 8/9, Rocky, Ubuntu 20.04+, Debian 11+, Alpine 3.18+ | x86 64, aarch64 ARM64 | Tier 1 Production | Native Binary, systemd, Container | Full support: privilege dropping --user , SIGHUP hot-reload, POSIX signal handling. | | Container / Kubernetes Docker, Podman, containerd, OpenShift, EKS, GKE | Linux x86 64, aarch64 | Tier 1 Production | OCI Image via multi-stage Dockerfile | Non-root UID 10001, native container health check. | | Windows Server 2016, 2019, 2022 & Windows 10/11 | x86 64 | Tier 2 Supported | Native Binary .exe , Task Scheduler, NSSM | Enforces set reuse address false . Note: --service flag is pending native SCM integration. | | macOS 12 Monterey, 13 Ventura, 14 Sonoma, 15 Sequoia | Apple Silicon M1/M2/M3/M4 , Intel x86 64 | Development / Testing | Native Binary cargo | Used for local development and diagnostic testing. | --- 2. Hardware and Resource Requirements Due to its zero-garbage-collection Rust architecture, PortProbe has extremely modest hardware requirements: Minimum Hardware: - CPU : 1 vCPU Core 2 Duo, AMD EPYC, AWS Graviton, or newer . - RAM : 64 MB available system RAM. - Disk Space : 20 MB of free storage for binary and log output. Recommended Production Hardware High Concurrency: 1,000+ sessions : - CPU : 2\u20134 vCPUs. - RAM : 512 MB available system RAM. - Network Interface : 1 Gbps or 10 Gbps Ethernet controller with hardware offloading enabled. --- 3. Toolchain & Build Prerequisites Source Builds If building PortProbe from source code, ensure the following developer tools are installed: 3.1 Rust Toolchain - Rust Version : 1.80.0 or later Rust 2021 Edition . - Cargo : Included with official Rust distributions. To check your current Rust installation: If Rust is not yet installed on your system, install it via the official installer: 3.2 Operating System Build Dependencies - Linux Debian / Ubuntu : - Linux RHEL / Rocky / AlmaLinux : - Alpine Linux : - Windows : - Microsoft C++ Build Tools via Visual Studio Installer or Build Tools for Visual Studio 2022 . --- 4. Network and Firewall Prerequisites Before starting PortProbe listeners or client probes: 1. Firewall Ingress Rules : Ensure host firewalls ufw , firewalld , iptables , Windows Defender Firewall permit incoming TCP traffic on the intended diagnostic port s e.g., TCP 8080 or the multi-port range configured . 2. Port Availability : Verify that no other local daemon Apache, Nginx, PostgreSQL, MySQL is currently bound to the target port: 3. Privileged Ports Warning 1024 : Binding to privileged ports e.g., 80, 443, 22 requires root privileges on Linux, or granting the CAP NET BIND SERVICE Linux capability. PortProbe includes automatic privilege dropping --user , --group to safely drop permissions post-binding."
