    "content": "Document Reference: PORTPROBE-DOC-UG-06 Document Version: 2.0.0 Classification: Comprehensive User Manual Status: Official Release Last Updated: November 2026 --- 1. Configuration Precedence Model PortProbe adheres to the standard three-tier enterprise configuration hierarchy: Precedence Rules: 1. Command-Line Arguments : Highest precedence. Any flag explicitly passed on the command line e.g., --bind 127.0.0.1 strictly overrides all file and environment values. 2. Environment Variables : Read automatically via Clap's env attribute e.g., PORTPROBE BIND . 3. Configuration File : Specified via -c / --config or PORTPROBE CONFIG . Unspecified CLI options are populated from the TOML file. 4. Hardcoded Secure Defaults : Unconfigured parameters are resolved to secure enterprise defaults bind = 127.0.0.1 , silent reject = true , hold open = false , timeout = 15s . --- 2. TOML Configuration File Schema PortProbe supports a declarative TOML configuration file typically installed at /etc/portprobe/portprobe.toml . --- 3. Secret Management & File Permissions PortProbe enforces strict security on cryptographic keys and bearer authentication tokens: Enforcing Permissions on POSIX Systems: When --admin-token-file or --tls-key is specified, PortProbe's verify file permissions inspects file metadata. - If permissions allow access by group or others mode & 0o077 != 0 , startup strictly fails with: - Remediation :"
