    "content": "Document Reference: PORTPROBE-DOC-UG-07 Document Version: 2.0.0 Classification: Comprehensive User Manual Status: Official Release Last Updated: November 2026 --- 1. Practical Recipe Collection Below are tested, ready-to-use command recipes for real-world enterprise infrastructure tasks. --- Recipe 1: Database Firewall Port Validation Oracle TCP 1521 Scenario : You requested the firewall team to open port 1521 between an App server 10.10.10.20 and a DB server 10.20.20.50 . The Oracle database is not yet installed. On DB Server 10.20.20.50 : On App Server 10.10.10.20 : Expected Output: --- Recipe 2: Multi-Port Web Proxy Verification Ports 80, 443, 8080\u20138085 Scenario : A DMZ reverse proxy needs to listen across multiple HTTP and backend microservice ports. Verifying all ports in a bash loop: --- Recipe 3: Strict Banking TLS 1.3-Only Encrypted Listener Scenario : Banking regulatory compliance requires all network traffic to be encrypted using TLS 1.3 exclusively with mTLS client certificate validation. Generate test certificates: Start PortProbe: Verify with TLS client probe: --- Recipe 4: Stress-Testing Load Balancer Concurrency Limits Scenario : Verify that an upstream load balancer correctly handles rate limiting when downstream traffic spikes. Clients exceeding 2 req/s will receive PORTPROBE: RATE LIMIT EXCEEDED\\n ."
