    "content": "Document Reference: PORTPROBE-DOC-REF-01 Document Version: 2.0.0 Classification: Reference Manual Status: Official Release Last Updated: November 2026 --- 1. CLI Command Overview PortProbe is invoked as a single unified executable: It operates in Daemon Mode by default, or in Client Probe Mode when --health-check is passed. --- 2. Quick-Reference Option Matrix | Flag / Option | Short | Environment Variable | Default | Valid Range / Values | Description | | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | | --port | -p | PORTPROBE PORT | None | 1 \u2013 65535 | Single TCP port to listen on or probe. | | --ports | | PORTPROBE PORTS | None | Comma-delimited list / ranges | Multiple ports / ranges e.g., 80,443,8080-8085 , max 50 ports . | | --bind | -b | PORTPROBE BIND | 127.0.0.1 | Valid IPv4 or IPv6 address | IP address to bind to daemon or target host IP health check . | | --timeout | -t | PORTPROBE TIMEOUT | 15 | 1 \u2013 3600 seconds | Connection lifetime before automatic termination. | | --max-connections | | PORTPROBE MAX CONNECTIONS | 100 | 1 \u2013 10000 | Maximum concurrent connections across all clients. | | --max-connections-per-ip | | PORTPROBE MAX CONNECTIONS PER IP | 10 | 1 \u2013 1000 | Maximum simultaneous connections from a single IP. | | --max-rate | | PORTPROBE MAX RATE | 20 | 1 \u2013 1000 req/s | Maximum accepted connections per second globally token bucket . | | --max-rate-per-ip | | PORTPROBE MAX RATE PER IP | 5 | 1 \u2013 1000 req/s | Maximum accepted connections per second per IP token bucket . | | --allow-cidr | | None | None | Comma-delimited CIDRs | Ingress subnet allowlist e.g., 10.0.0.0/8,192.168.1.0/24 . | | --silent-reject | | PORTPROBE SILENT REJECT | true | true , false | Silently drop rejected connections without diagnostic banners. | | --hold-open | | PORTPROBE HOLD OPEN | false | true , false | Keep TCP socket open post-response until timeout expires. | | --config | -c | PORTPROBE CONFIG | None | Valid file path | Path to TOML configuration file e.g., /etc/portprobe/portprobe.toml . | | --log-format | | PORTPROBE LOG FORMAT | text | text , json | Log output format for terminal viewing or SIEM ingestion. | | --health-check | | None | false | Boolean flag | Execute active client healthcheck against configured bind and port. | | --health-check-tls | | None | false | Boolean flag | Connect with TLS encryption during client healthcheck. | | --health-check-domain | | None | localhost | Valid hostname / SNI | Expected TLS domain name / SNI for healthcheck certificate verification. | | --health-check-ca | | None | None | Valid file path | Path to custom CA certificate PEM bundle for healthcheck TLS validation. | | --admin-port | | PORTPROBE ADMIN PORT | None | 1 \u2013 65535 | Localhost port for Prometheus /metrics and /healthz HTTP server. | | --admin-token | | PORTPROBE ADMIN TOKEN | None | String | Bearer token for authenticating admin endpoint deprecated on CLI . | | --admin-token-file | | PORTPROBE ADMIN TOKEN FILE | None | Valid file path | Path to file containing Bearer token with 0600 / 0400 permissions. | | --tls-min-version | | PORTPROBE TLS MIN VERSION | 1.2 | 1.2 , 1.3 | Minimum TLS version 1.3 enforces strict TLS 1.3 only . | | --tls-cert | | PORTPROBE TLS CERT | None | Valid file path | Path to TLS server certificate chain PEM file. | | --tls-key | | PORTPROBE TLS KEY | None | Valid file path | Path to TLS server private key PEM file enforces 0600 / 0400 . | | --tls-client-ca | | PORTPROBE TLS CLIENT CA | None | Valid file path | Path to CA bundle for mutual TLS mTLS client verification. | | --user | | PORTPROBE USER | None | Valid POSIX user | Unprivileged user account to drop privileges to post-bind. | | --group | | PORTPROBE GROUP | None | Valid POSIX group | Unprivileged group account to drop privileges to post-bind. | | --service | | None | false | Boolean flag | Run as background Windows Service Operational Workaround: NSSM . | | --help | -h | None | None | None | Print help information. | | --version | -V | None | None | None | Print version information. | --- 3. Detailed Parameter Specifications -p, --port PORT - Description : Specifies the TCP port to listen on in Daemon mode, or the target port to probe in Client mode. - Accepted Values : Integer 1 to 65535 . - Validation : Rejects 0 or values 65535 . Either --port or --ports must be provided. --ports PORTS - Description : Comma-separated list or ranges of TCP ports for multi-port listening. - Example : --ports \"80,443,8080-8085\" - Constraints : Maximum range span of 100 ports per item; maximum of 50 total unique listening sockets. -b, --bind BIND - Description : In Daemon mode, the IP address to bind to. In Client mode, the remote destination IP to probe. - Default : 127.0.0.1 . - Accepted Values : Valid IPv4 e.g., 0.0.0.0 , 192.168.1.10 or IPv6 address e.g., :: , 2001:db8::1 . --admin-token-file PATH - Description : Path to a file containing the secret Bearer token used to authenticate /metrics and /healthz . - Security Check : Enforces POSIX perm"
