    "content": "Document Reference: PORTPROBE-DOC-DEV-02 Document Version: 2.0.0 Classification: Developer Manual Status: Official Release Last Updated: November 2026 --- 1. Local Development Workflows 1.1 Building 1.2 Code Formatting & Linting --- 2. Test Execution & Regression Suite PortProbe contains 81 automated unit and integration tests testing all aspects of the CLI, admission control, and server engines: Run All Tests: Run Tests with Verbose Output: Test Suite Structure: - cli::tests : Tests timeout validation, concurrency bounds, CIDR IPv4/IPv6 parsing, dual-stack IPv4-mapped IPv6 subnets, multi-port expansion, port deduplication, config file merging, and CLI override precedence. - server::tests : Tests token-bucket refill calculations, per-IP rate limiting isolation, mutex poisoning recovery, hold-open payload draining caps, silent rejection, SIGHUP CIDR updates, admin server Bearer token validation, Slowloris header caps 4KB , idle connection timeouts, and client health checks. --- 3. Security Auditing & Supply Chain Verification --- 4. Continuous Integration CI Pipeline PortProbe's GitHub Actions pipeline .github/workflows/ci.yml enforces five mandatory quality gates: 1. lint-and-format : Checks cargo fmt and cargo clippy -D warnings . 2. test : Matrix execution across ubuntu-latest , windows-latest , and macos-latest . 3. security : Executes cargo audit , cargo deny check , and generates CycloneDX SBOM. 4. container-security : Builds Alpine container and runs Aquasecurity Trivy scanner, failing on CRITICAL or HIGH vulnerabilities. 5. security-regression-gates : Greps src/ to verify zero unsafe blocks and zero variable-time token comparisons. 6. release-provenance : Attests releases via Sigstore Cosign on tagged builds v ."
