    "content": "Document Reference: PORTPROBE-DOC-DEV-03 Document Version: 2.0.0 Classification: Developer Manual Status: Official Release Last Updated: November 2026 --- 1. Contribution Principles We welcome contributions to PortProbe! Before submitting code, please review these guidelines to ensure quality, performance, and security. Guiding Principles: - No Unsafe Code : The repository strictly forbids unsafe code blocks. - Test-Driven Hardening : Every bug fix, new configuration option, or security patch must include corresponding unit tests in src/cli.rs or src/server.rs . - Backward Compatibility : Existing CLI flags and TOML configuration parameters must remain stable across minor releases. --- 2. Pull Request Submission Checklist Before submitting a Pull Request PR : - Code passes formatting check: cargo fmt --all -- --check - Code passes Clippy: cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings - All automated tests pass: cargo test --all-targets 139 tests - Security audit passes: cargo audit and cargo deny check - Zero unsafe blocks present in src/ - Documentation updated in docs/ if modifying flags or behaviors. --- 3. Reporting Security Vulnerabilities If you discover a security vulnerability or potential denial-of-service issue in PortProbe: - Do not open a public GitHub issue. - Submit details through GitHub Private Vulnerability Reporting or contact the security team directly. - Include a minimal reproducible test case demonstrating the vulnerability."
