    "content": "Document Reference: PORTPROBE-DOC-REL-03 Document Version: 2.0.0 Classification: Enterprise Strategic Roadmap Status: Official Release Last Updated: November 2026 --- 1. Roadmap Evolution & Planned Capabilities The PortProbe product roadmap outlines planned enhancements across upcoming minor and major releases: --- 2. Release Milestones & Feature Breakdown Version 2.1.0 Q1 2027 - Native Windows Service Dispatcher : Integrate windows-service crate to link --service directly to the Windows Service Control Manager SCM . - TLS on Administrative Endpoint : Add --admin-tls to allow secure remote Prometheus scraping over HTTPS. - Windows NTFS DACL Validation : Native Win32 API checks verifying that secret token files are accessible only by the service owner. Version 2.2.0 Q2 2027 - UDP Connectivity Verification : Support UDP echo/diagnostic listeners and client probing. - DNS Resolution Probing : Active validation of split-horizon DNS, SRV records, and reverse lookups. - OpenTelemetry OTel Native Tracing : Export distributed trace spans for connection lifecycle diagnostics. Version 3.0.0 Q4 2027 - PortProbe Mesh Coordinator : Centralized coordination daemon aggregating distributed probe results across multi-cloud VPCs. - Kubernetes Custom Resource Definition CRD & Operator : Automate canary probe deployment across Kubernetes clusters."
